{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-39001" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} & -2 \\\\ -\\text{i} & 5+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$, find the result of applying to $A$ the following elementary row operation:\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{\\text{i}}{1-\\text{i}}{R}_{1}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "71c5988b546782b661e873fcf13dd436879ebc5a47dfb3e048d57ef4cc989226"} {"question" "q-39001" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's apply the row operations to $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} & -2 \\\\ -\\text{i} & 5+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{\\text{i}}{1-\\text{i}}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} & -2 \\\\ -\\text{i}+\\frac{\\text{i}(1-\\text{i})}{1-\\text{i}} & 5+\\text{i}-\\frac{2\\text{i}}{1-\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} & -2 \\\\ -\\text{i}+\\text{i} & \\frac{(5+\\text{i})\\cdot (1-\\text{i})-2\\text{i}}{1-\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} & -2 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the result  is \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} & -2 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "71c5988b546782b661e873fcf13dd436879ebc5a47dfb3e048d57ef4cc989226"} {"question" "q-39001" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d3f16b3f0ecf8d5873283e7befb470a63cdb8b0e929f123a22619c642147266d"} {"question" "q-39001" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "71c5988b546782b661e873fcf13dd436879ebc5a47dfb3e048d57ef4cc989226"} {"question" "q-39001" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ -\\text{i} & 5+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ -\\text{i} & 5+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} & -2 \\\\ 0 & 6+i\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} & -2 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "71c5988b546782b661e873fcf13dd436879ebc5a47dfb3e048d57ef4cc989226"} {"question" "q-39001" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} & -2 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "71c5988b546782b661e873fcf13dd436879ebc5a47dfb3e048d57ef4cc989226"} {"question" "q-76201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $\\,\\text{Re}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\text{Im}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}e & f \\\\ g & h\\end{aligned}]\\,$ are the real and imaginary parts of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2-3\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ 1+\\text{i} & 5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ then what is the value of $cd+gh?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "71c5988b546782b661e873fcf13dd436879ebc5a47dfb3e048d57ef4cc989226"} {"question" "q-76201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For the given matrix $A,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2-3\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ 1+\\text{i} & 5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2-3\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ 1+\\text{i} & 0+5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(A)}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(A)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $c=1,d=0,g=1$ and $h=5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\ncd+gh=1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 5=5.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "71c5988b546782b661e873fcf13dd436879ebc5a47dfb3e048d57ef4cc989226"} {"question" "q-76201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d3f16b3f0ecf8d5873283e7befb470a63cdb8b0e929f123a22619c642147266d"} {"question" "q-76201" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "71c5988b546782b661e873fcf13dd436879ebc5a47dfb3e048d57ef4cc989226"} {"question" "q-76201" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "71c5988b546782b661e873fcf13dd436879ebc5a47dfb3e048d57ef4cc989226"} {"question" "q-76201" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "71c5988b546782b661e873fcf13dd436879ebc5a47dfb3e048d57ef4cc989226"} {"question" "q-76202" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $\\,\\text{Re}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\text{Im}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}e & f \\\\ g & h\\end{aligned}]\\,$ are the real and imaginary parts of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 1-6\\text{i} \\\\ 3+\\text{i} & 4+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ then what is the value of $bc+eg?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "71c5988b546782b661e873fcf13dd436879ebc5a47dfb3e048d57ef4cc989226"} {"question" "q-76202" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For the given matrix $A,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 1-6\\text{i} \\\\ 3+\\text{i} & 4+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8+0\\text{i} & 1-6\\text{i} \\\\ 3+\\text{i} & 4+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}8 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(A)}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}0 & -6 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(A)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $b=1,c=3,e=0$ and $g=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nbc+eg=1\\cdot 3+0\\cdot 1=3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "71c5988b546782b661e873fcf13dd436879ebc5a47dfb3e048d57ef4cc989226"} {"question" "q-76202" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d3f16b3f0ecf8d5873283e7befb470a63cdb8b0e929f123a22619c642147266d"} {"question" "q-76202" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "71c5988b546782b661e873fcf13dd436879ebc5a47dfb3e048d57ef4cc989226"} {"question" "q-76202" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "11"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "71c5988b546782b661e873fcf13dd436879ebc5a47dfb3e048d57ef4cc989226"} {"question" "q-76202" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "71c5988b546782b661e873fcf13dd436879ebc5a47dfb3e048d57ef4cc989226"} {"question" "q-140329" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}-3+5\\text{i} & 4-3\\text{i} \\\\ -4\\text{i} & 5-5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-3\\text{i} \\\\ 4-5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$, then $\\,Ax=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "71c5988b546782b661e873fcf13dd436879ebc5a47dfb3e048d57ef4cc989226"} {"question" "q-140329" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying the matrix by the vector using the usual method, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}-3+5\\text{i} & 4-3\\text{i} \\\\ -4\\text{i} & 5-5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3\\text{i} \\\\ 4-5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(-3+5\\text{i})(-3\\text{i})+(4-3\\text{i})(4-5\\text{i}) \\\\ (-4\\text{i})(-3\\text{i})+(5-5\\text{i})(4-5\\text{i})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(15+9\\text{i})+(1-32\\text{i}) \\\\ (-12)+(-5-45\\text{i})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16-23\\text{i} \\\\ -17-45\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "71c5988b546782b661e873fcf13dd436879ebc5a47dfb3e048d57ef4cc989226"} {"question" "q-140329" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d3f16b3f0ecf8d5873283e7befb470a63cdb8b0e929f123a22619c642147266d"} {"question" "q-140329" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "71c5988b546782b661e873fcf13dd436879ebc5a47dfb3e048d57ef4cc989226"} {"question" "q-140329" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-17-45\\text{i} \\\\ 16-23\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}10+51\\text{i} \\\\ 24-20\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}16-23\\text{i} \\\\ -17-45\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}16-27\\text{i} \\\\ 23-35\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}24-20\\text{i} \\\\ 10+51\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "71c5988b546782b661e873fcf13dd436879ebc5a47dfb3e048d57ef4cc989226"} {"question" "q-140329" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}16-23\\text{i} \\\\ -17-45\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "71c5988b546782b661e873fcf13dd436879ebc5a47dfb3e048d57ef4cc989226"} {"question" "q-140381" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} & -2-4\\text{i} \\\\ 3-2\\text{i} & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$, find the result of applying to $A$ the following  elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}=\\frac{1}{1+2\\text{i}}{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}={R}_{2}+(2\\text{i}-3){R}_{1}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "71c5988b546782b661e873fcf13dd436879ebc5a47dfb3e048d57ef4cc989226"} {"question" "q-140381" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's apply the row operations to $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} & -2-4\\text{i} \\\\ 3-2\\text{i} & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{1+2\\text{i}}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3-2\\text{i} & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(2\\text{i}-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 6-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the result is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 6-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "71c5988b546782b661e873fcf13dd436879ebc5a47dfb3e048d57ef4cc989226"} {"question" "q-140381" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d3f16b3f0ecf8d5873283e7befb470a63cdb8b0e929f123a22619c642147266d"} {"question" "q-140381" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "71c5988b546782b661e873fcf13dd436879ebc5a47dfb3e048d57ef4cc989226"} {"question" "q-140381" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\text{i}-3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 6-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\text{i}-3\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "71c5988b546782b661e873fcf13dd436879ebc5a47dfb3e048d57ef4cc989226"} {"question" "q-140381" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 6-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070700/state.json" "file_sha256" "71c5988b546782b661e873fcf13dd436879ebc5a47dfb3e048d57ef4cc989226"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2508 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
